    "narrative": "Our offensive outlook for today is headlined by two high-upside plays in favorable hitting environments. **Dylan Beavers** (68.38) and **Geraldo Perdomo** (68.19) are our strongest starts. **Dylan Beavers** benefits significantly from a park factor boost (+16%) and a high-probability matchup against L\u00f3pez, while **Geraldo Perdomo** gains efficiency from his elevated spot at the top of the order (+8%) and a prime opportunity to capitalize on Mikolas\u2019s mediocre stuff. **Bryce Harper** (67.44) also remains an essential start despite the matchup against Warren; his elite xwOBA profile and the favorable wind conditions ensure he remains a cornerstone of our lineup even if we are officially waiting on his lineup confirmation.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today involved **JJ Bleday**, whose 46.72 score was the highest of our benched players. While **JJ Bleday** offered a respectable baseline, the optimizer ultimately pivoted to **Daulton Varsho** (47.78). Although **Daulton Varsho** faces a tough LHP matchup, he remains in the lineup due to his aggressive base-running profile; against a pitcher with slow delivery metrics, his potential for a stolen base\u2014our scarcest category\u2014provided just enough of a mathematical edge to surpass **JJ Bleday**. We are also keeping a close eye on risk factors: **Cal Raleigh** (44.02) is our most precarious start, as he faces the formidable deGrom, whose presence significantly suppresses our ceiling today. Additionally, we are proceeding with **Luis Arraez** and **Jung Hoo Lee** under the assumption of their standard lineup slots; should either be dropped down the order, their projections will require immediate re-evaluation.",
